342 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 267 0 R/E(The United Nations Office on Drugs and Crime \(UNODC\) is a UN body dedicated to combating illicit drugs, transnational organized crime, corruption, terrorism, and other emerging security threats. Through international cooperation, policy development, research, and technical assistance, UNODC supports Member States in strengthening justice systems, preventing crime, and protecting communities. As criminal networks increasingly operate across borders and exploit new technologies, the committee provides a platform for delegates to develop effective, cooperative, and sustainable solutions to these complex global challenges.)/Pg 12 0 R/K[6]>>
