354 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 267 0 R/E(The Security Council is one of the six principal organs of the United Nations. Article 24 of the Charter assigns it primary responsibility for the maintenance of international peace and security. The Council\220s composition and voting rules are established in Chapter V.)/Pg 12 0 R/K[18]>>
endobj

355 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 267 0 R/T(Why the Council is different from a GA committee)/E(Why the Council is different from a GA committee)/Pg 12 0 R/K[19]>>
endobj

356 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 267 0 R/E(The Council is smaller, faster and more power-sensitive. A persuasive speech is useful, but a proposal must account for veto politics, mandate limits, state consent, implementation capacity and the interests of actors outside the room.)/Pg 12 0 R/K[20]>>
endobj

