389 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 268 0 R/E(The Council must respond to threats while operating inside a political system where the strongest states may disagree. The result is often compromise: a resolution may be less ambitious than the initial draft but more implementable because it preserves minimum consensus.)/Pg 13 0 R/K[16]>>
endobj

390 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 268 0 R/T(The Council\220s central tension)/E(The Council\220s central tension)/Pg 13 0 R/K[17]>>
endobj

391 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 268 0 R/T(2. Funding of the United Nations Security Council)/E(2. Funding of the United Nations Security Council)/Pg 13 0 R/K[18]>>
endobj

392 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 268 0 R/E(The Security Council does not operate as an independently funded institution with its own standalone budget. Its authority is exercised through the wider United Nations financial system, while specific Council-authorized activities, especially peacekeeping operations and special political missions, are financed through mechanisms approved by the General Assembly)/Pg 13 0 R/K[19]>>
endobj

393 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 268 0 R/T(How the Council is funded)/E(How the Council is funded)/Pg 13 0 R/K[20]>>
endobj

394 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 268 0 R/T(Peacekeeping financing)/E(Peacekeeping financing)/Pg 13 0 R/K[21]>>
endobj

395 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 268 0 R/E(Under Article 17 of the Charter, the General Assembly considers and approves the Organization\220s budget and apportions expenses among Member States. Peacekeeping operations are financed separately from the regular UN budget through assessments, with Member States collectively responsible for the expenses. The scale for peacekeeping gives the permanent members a higher share because of their special responsibility for international peace and security.)/Pg 13 0 R/K[22]>>
endobj

