endobj

434 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 269 0 R/E(4.Political feasibility: Is there a pathway to nine votes and, where substantive, sufficient P5 acceptance?)/Pg 14 0 R/K[22]>>
endobj

435 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 269 0 R/E(5.Implementation: Who will actually carry out the decision?)/Pg 14 0 R/K[23]>>
endobj

436 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 269 0 R/E(Applying the filter is harder than listing it. A crisis can satisfy the mandate test on paper while failing the political-feasibility test in practice: many humanitarian emergencies plausibly threaten peace and security, but a topic involving a permanent member's direct interests, or one where another organ already has clear lead responsibility, may not be where the Council can add distinctive value. Strong delegates apply all five criteria together rather than stopping once the first one is satisfied.)/Pg 14 0 R/K[24]>>
endobj

437 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 269 0 R/E(The actionability test deserves particular care in an open-agenda committee. It is not enough that the Council has used a tool such as sanctions or peacekeeping mandates before; delegates should be able to )/Pg 14 0 R/K[25]>>
endobj

438 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 269 0 R/T(The five-part filter)/E(The five-part filter)/Pg 14 0 R/K[26]>>
endobj

