471 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 270 0 R/E(name which specific tool fits the crisis at hand and explain, in concrete terms, who would implement it, with what resources, and under whose authority. A resolution that cannot answer this in a moderated caucus is vulnerable to the same drafting weaknesses covered later in this guide's implementation and QARMA sections.)/Pg 15 0 R/K[16]>>
endobj

472 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 270 0 R/E(Delegates should also test their chosen crisis against recent Council practice: has the issue appeared on the Council's agenda before, and if so, what happened to earlier resolutions or presidential statements on it? A topic with a documented history of Council engagement, existing reporting mechanisms or a standing sanctions committee is usually easier to build a workable resolution around than one the Council has never addressed, because delegates can extend or adjust existing tools rather than inventing an entirely new mandate from nothing.)/Pg 15 0 R/K[17]>>
endobj

