endobj

686 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 275 0 R/E(That cooperative period also produced a major expansion in what the Council was willing to do under Chapter VII: the ad hoc international criminal tribunals for the former Yugoslavia \(1993\) and Rwanda \(1994\), an increasingly assertive use of sanctions regimes, and peacekeeping mandates that began to include explicit civilian-protection language rather than pure ceasefire monitoring. Veto use rose again after 2011, driven substantially by Russian and Chinese vetoes on Syria, illustrating that the Council's tools have not fundamentally changed since the Charter was signed, but the political conditions for using them have continued to fluctuate.)/Pg 20 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

687 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 275 0 R/T(1.4. Relevant International and Regional Frameworks)/E(1.4. Relevant International and Regional Frameworks)/Pg 20 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

688 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 275 0 R/T(Chapter VI \204 peaceful settlement)/E(Chapter VI \204 peaceful settlement)/Pg 20 0 R/K[11]>>
endobj

689 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 275 0 R/E(Chapter VI focuses on peaceful settlement of disputes. The Council can investigate situations, call upon parties to settle disputes and recommend procedures or terms. Chapter VI measures are generally recommendation-oriented.)/Pg 20 0 R/K[12]>>
endobj

690 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 275 0 R/T(Chapter VII \204 threats to peace)/E(Chapter VII \204 threats to peace)/Pg 20 0 R/K[13]>>
endobj

691 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 275 0 R/E(Chapter VII is the legal framework most closely associated with the Council\220s enforcement authority. Article 39 provides the threshold determination of a threat to the peace, breach of the peace or act of aggression. Article 41 permits measures not involving armed force, including sanctions, while Article 42 concerns action involving armed force when Article 41 measures are inadequate. The Council\220s Repertoire documents how these provisions have actually been interpreted and applied over time.)/Pg 20 0 R/K[14]>>
endobj

