723 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 276 0 R/E(mun@umt.edu.pk)/Pg 21 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

724 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 276 0 R/E(umt_mun)/Pg 21 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

725 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 276 0 R/E(The UN Charter is the primary legal framework for Security Council action. Article 24 assigns the Council primary responsibility for the maintenance of international peace and security; Article 25 requires Member States to accept and carry out Council decisions. Chapter VI addresses peaceful settlement, while Chapter VII provides enforcement powers. Chapter VIII recognizes a role for regional arrangements in maintaining peace and security.)/Pg 21 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

726 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 276 0 R/T(Chapter VIII \204 regional arrangements)/E(Chapter VIII \204 regional arrangements)/Pg 21 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

727 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 276 0 R/T(United Nations Charter)/E(United Nations Charter)/Pg 21 0 R/K[11]>>
endobj

728 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 276 0 R/T(International Humanitarian Law and Protection of Civilians)/E(International Humanitarian Law and Protection of Civilians)/Pg 21 0 R/K[12]>>
endobj

729 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 276 0 R/E(Where armed conflict is involved, Council action should be read alongside the rules of international humanitarian law concerning distinction, proportionality, precautions in attack, protection of civilians and civilian objects, and humanitarian relief. Resolution drafting should avoid creating mechanisms that weaken these protections.)/Pg 21 0 R/K[13]>>
endobj

730 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 276 0 R/T(Women, Peace and Security)/E(Women, Peace and Security)/Pg 21 0 R/K[14]>>
endobj

731 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 276 0 R/E(Security Council Resolution 1325 \(2000\) and the subsequent Women, Peace and Security resolutions establish a framework for women\220s participation in peace processes and for addressing conflict-related risks to women and girls. Delegates should consider participation, protection and prevention when designing peace and security measures.)/Pg 21 0 R/K[15]>>
endobj

