763 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 277 0 R/E(mun@umt.edu.pk)/Pg 22 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

764 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 277 0 R/E(umt_mun)/Pg 22 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

765 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 277 0 R/E(When a crisis involves shipping or chokepoints such as the Strait of Hormuz, delegates should distinguish Security Council authority from the separate rules of international maritime law. Council measures should address navigation, civilian shipping and escalation risks without treating maritime questions as purely military issues.)/Pg 22 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

766 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 277 0 R/T(Maritime Security and the Law of the Sea)/E(Maritime Security and the Law of the Sea)/Pg 22 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

767 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 277 0 R/T(Nuclear Non-Proliferation and IAEA Verification)/E(Nuclear Non-Proliferation and IAEA Verification)/Pg 22 0 R/K[11]>>
endobj

768 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 277 0 R/E(Where armed conflict is involved, Council action should be read alongside the rules of international humanitarian law concerning distinction, proportionality, precautions in attack, protection of civilians and civilian objects, and humanitarian relief. Resolution drafting should avoid creating mechanisms that weaken these protections.)/Pg 22 0 R/K[12]>>
endobj

769 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 277 0 R/T(Regional organizations and Chapter VIII)/E(Regional organizations and Chapter VIII)/Pg 22 0 R/K[13]>>
endobj

770 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 277 0 R/E(Regional organizations have become increasingly important partners in conflict prevention, mediation and peace operations. Chapter VIII recognizes a role for regional arrangements, and Security Council practice includes cases where the Council has authorized or supported regional operations and requested reporting from regional organizations. The African Union is particularly significant in this regard because many African conflicts require both continental political engagement and international legitimacy/resources.)/Pg 22 0 R/K[14]>>
endobj

771 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 277 0 R/E(The relationship is not simply hierarchical. Regional organizations may have greater political familiarity, proximity and legitimacy with the parties to a conflict, while the UN can provide broader diplomatic legitimacy, financing mechanisms or authorization under the Charter. Effective cooperation therefore depends on )/Pg 22 0 R/K[15]>>
endobj

772 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 277 0 R/T(Chapter VIII in practice)/E(Chapter VIII in practice)/Pg 22 0 R/K[16]>>
endobj

