800 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 278 0 R/T(1. Mandate of the United Nations Security Council)/E(1. Mandate of the United Nations Security Council)/Pg 23 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

801 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 278 0 R/E(The United Nations Office on Drugs and Crime \(UNODC\) is a UN body dedicated to combating illicit drugs, transnational organized crime, corruption, terrorism, and other emerging security threats. Through international cooperation, policy development, research, and technical assistance, UNODC supports Member States in strengthening justice systems, preventing crime, and protecting communities. As criminal networks increasingly operate across borders and exploit new technologies, the committee provides a platform for delegates to develop effective, cooperative, and sustainable solutions to these complex global challenges.)/Pg 23 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

802 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 278 0 R/T(Purpose and composition)/E(Purpose and composition)/Pg 23 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

803 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 278 0 R/Pg 23 0 R/A[1590 0 R 0]/K[6]>>
endobj

804 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 278 0 R/E(mun@umt.edu.pk)/Pg 23 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

805 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 278 0 R/E(umt_mun)/Pg 23 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

806 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 278 0 R/E(coordination rather than assuming that one institution can replace the other.)/Pg 23 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

807 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 278 0 R/E(Regional organizations can provide proximity, political legitimacy and specialized knowledge. The African Union, European Union, Arab League, ASEAN-related mechanisms and other regional structures have different legal bases and capabilities.)/Pg 23 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

808 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 278 0 R/T(Why regional ownership matters)/E(Why regional ownership matters)/Pg 23 0 R/K[11]>>
endobj

809 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 278 0 R/E(\267Neighbouring states often understand local political and economic incentives better.)/Pg 23 0 R/K[12]>>
endobj

810 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 278 0 R/E(\267Regional mediators may have access to parties unavailable to distant actors.)/Pg 23 0 R/K[13]>>
endobj

811 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 278 0 R/E(\267Regional organizations can support ceasefire monitoring or stabilization.)/Pg 23 0 R/K[14]>>
endobj

812 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 278 0 R/E(\267Regional sanctions and diplomatic pressure can complement UN action.)/Pg 23 0 R/K[15]>>
endobj

813 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 278 0 R/T(The coordination problem)/E(The coordination problem)/Pg 23 0 R/K[16]>>
endobj

814 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 278 0 R/E(Multiple mediators can create duplication or contradictory incentives. A strong Council resolution should therefore specify coordination channels, reporting arrangements and division of labour where appropriate.)/Pg 23 0 R/K[17]>>
endobj

815 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 278 0 R/T(Article 41 measures)/E(Article 41 measures)/Pg 23 0 R/K[18]>>
endobj

816 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 278 0 R/E(Security Council sanctions have evolved substantially. Earlier regimes sometimes imposed broad economic restrictions, while later practice increasingly emphasized targeted measures against particular individuals, entities, commodities or activities. The Council currently describes sanctions as one of its enforcement tools under Article 41 and notes that they may include arms embargoes, travel bans and financial restrictions.)/Pg 23 0 R/K[19]>>
endobj

817 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 278 0 R/E(The historical evolution also reflects lessons about humanitarian effects and implementation. Sanctions are not automatically effective simply because they are legally binding. Their impact depends on monitoring, domestic implementation, exemptions, enforcement capacity and the willingness of States and private actors to comply. The Council\220s own practice recognizes that sanctions are generally more effective when embedded in a broader strategy of peacekeeping, peacemaking and peacebuilding.)/Pg 23 0 R/K[20]>>
endobj

818 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 278 0 R/Pg 23 0 R/A[1617 0 R 0]/K[21]>>
endobj

