endobj

938 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 281 0 R/E(The Rwandan genocide is one of the most important historical cases for understanding the consequences of inadequate international response. In 1994, mass killing unfolded while the UN peacekeeping operation in Rwanda, UNAMIR, operated under a limited mandate and faced severe political and operational constraints. The international response failed to prevent or halt the genocide, and the experience became a lasting reference point in debates over civilian protection, early warning and the responsibilities of the international community.)/Pg 26 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

939 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 281 0 R/T(Srebrenica, 1995)/E(Srebrenica, 1995)/Pg 26 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

940 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 281 0 R/E(Srebrenica demonstrated another dimension of the protection problem. The UN had declared Srebrenica a safe area and deployed UNPROFOR personnel, yet Bosnian Serb forces captured the enclave in July 1995 and subsequently murdered thousands of Bosniak men and boys. The episode exposed the gap that can arise between a political designation such as a \215safe area\216 and the resources and authority required to enforce that protection.Srebrenica illustrates the danger of declaring a protected area without the political, military and operational capacity required to protect civilians. It is particularly useful for studying mandate credibility and the relationship between peacekeeping and coercive force.)/Pg 26 0 R/K[11]>>
endobj

941 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 281 0 R/E(HyHybrid and jointly supported mechanisms in Africa demonstrate both the potential and complexity of partnership. Financing, command arrangements, political alignment and accountability must be addressed rather than assumed.)/Pg 26 0 R/K[12]>>
endobj

942 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 281 0 R/T(African Union\205UN cooperation)/E(African Union\205UN cooperation)/Pg 26 0 R/K[13]>>
endobj

943 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 281 0 R/T(ISIL/Al-Qaida sanctions)/E(ISIL/Al-Qaida sanctions)/Pg 26 0 R/K[14]>>
endobj

944 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 281 0 R/E(TThe 1267/1989/2253 regime demonstrates how the Council can combine targeted assets freezes, travel bans and arms embargoes with a sanctions list, monitoring team and delisting procedures. It also illustrates the continuing challenge of due process, evidence, implementation and changing threat networks.)/Pg 26 0 R/K[15]>>
endobj

945 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 281 0 R/T(Rwanda, 1994)/E(Rwanda, 1994)/Pg 26 0 R/K[16]>>
