1056 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 284 0 R/T(Veto politics and Council paralysis)/E(Veto politics and Council paralysis)/Pg 29 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

1057 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 284 0 R/E(The Council can adopt strong language yet fail to act when a permanent member\220s interests are directly implicated. This creates a mandate-capacity gap between what the Council formally decides and what it can politically enforce.)/Pg 29 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

1058 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 284 0 R/E(hree Iranian vessels after Iran launched ballistic missiles at two U.S. Navy ships. These developments demonstrate how quickly a partially negotiated ceasefire or de-escalation framework can unravel when verification, compFor MUN delegates, the central questions are not simply which side is \215right.\216 The case should be analyzed through the Council\220s actual mandate: What evidence establishes a threat to international peace and security? How should competing Article 51 claims be assessed? What mechanism could verify a ceasefire? How can freedom of navigation be protected without widening the war? What sanctions, humanitarian exemptions and monitoring arrangements are realistic? How can nuclear verification be linked to diplomacy? Which regional actors can mediate? And what consequences can the Council credibly attach to non-compliance without making escalation more likely?)/Pg 29 0 R/K[11]>>
endobj

1059 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 284 0 R/E(liance and dispute-resolution mechanisms are insufficiently trusted or enforced.)/Pg 29 0 R/K[12]>>
endobj

1060 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 284 0 R/T(1.7. Challenges in the Implementation and Enforcement)/E(1.7. Challenges in the Implementation and Enforcement)/Pg 29 0 R/K[13]>>
endobj

1061 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 284 0 R/T(Mandate-capacity gaps)/E(Mandate-capacity gaps)/Pg 29 0 R/K[14]>>
endobj

1062 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 284 0 R/E(Peacekeeping and political missions depend on personnel, financing, host-state cooperation and operational capacity. A mandate that promises more than these resources can support risks creating expectations that cannot be met.)/Pg 29 0 R/K[15]>>
endobj

1063 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 284 0 R/Pg 29 0 R/A[1617 0 R 0]/K[16]>>
endobj

