1139 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 286 0 R/T(Resolution 2664 \204 a standing humanitarian exemption)/E(Resolution 2664 \204 a standing humanitarian exemption)/Pg 31 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

1140 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 286 0 R/E(On 9 December 2022 the Council adopted resolution 2664, creating a standing humanitarian exemption that applies across nearly all United Nations sanctions regimes rather than requiring a bespoke carve-out for each new measure. The resolution, adopted 14 in favour with one abstention \(India\), provides that the provision, processing or payment of funds and the provision of goods and services necessary to ensure the timely delivery of humanitarian assistance or to support other activities that support basic human needs are permitted and do not violate Council-imposed asset freezes. For the 1267/1989/2253 ISIL \(Da'esh\) and Al-Qaida regime the exemption initially applied for a two-year period; the Council subsequently reaffirmed its continued application through resolution 2761 \(2024\).)/Pg 31 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

1141 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 286 0 R/E(The exemption is deliberately not unconditional. Humanitarian providers are still expected to use reasonable efforts to minimize any benefit to designated individuals or entities, and the resolution requires the UN Emergency Relief Coordinator to brief the relevant sanctions committees roughly once a year on how the exemption is being used in practice. This pairing of a broad legal permission with a recurring accountability mechanism is a useful drafting model: delegates designing or reviewing a sanctions regime can build humanitarian protection in from the outset rather than negotiating waivers case by case after harm has already occurred.)/Pg 31 0 R/K[11]>>
endobj

1142 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 286 0 R/E(elsewhere in the financial system, and it can quietly strip humanitarian operations of banking access even where an exemption technically exists on paper.)/Pg 31 0 R/K[12]>>
endobj

1143 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 286 0 R/T(Why unintended effects still occur)/E(Why unintended effects still occur)/Pg 31 0 R/K[13]>>
endobj

1144 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 286 0 R/E(Even with a standing exemption in place, unintended effects can persist because individual banks and private companies, not the Council itself, ultimately decide whether to process a given transaction, and many still choose caution over risk. A well-drafted resolution should therefore go beyond the legal exemption and address practical implementation: clear guidance for financial institutions and )/Pg 31 0 R/K[14]>>
endobj

